Fix 2 — Update dotenv.config() in server.js
Since your file is config/config.env not .env, you need to tell dotenv the correct path:
jsconst dotenv = require('dotenv');

// ✅ Point to correct file location
dotenv.config({ path: './config/config.env' });

Fix 3 — Remove config.env from GitHub if Already Pushed
bashgit rm --cached backend/config/config.env
git add .
git commit -m "fix: remove config.env from tracking"
git push

Verify It's Working
bash# Check if file is ignored
git check-ignore -v backend/config/config.env
Should show:
.gitignore:3:config.env    backend/config/config.env ✅

Your config.env Should Look Like This
envMONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://username:password@cluster0.xxxxx.mongodb.net/mini-crm?retryWrites=true&w=majority
JWT_SECRET=your_super_secret_key_here
PORT=5000
NODE_ENV=production
CLIENT_URL=https://your-app.vercel.app


The key fix is dotenv.config({ path: './config/config.env' }) — without the correct path, dotenv can't find your variables and they come up as undefined! This was likely the root cause of all your earlier MongoDB URI errors! 🎯
